{
 "text": "Hey there, it's James and Christina, your missionaries with Wycliffe Bible Translators. The last several months have been full, and it's exciting to be able to share what God has been doing in our family, our Wycliffe ministry, and in Bible translation around the world. First, a family update. After six months of in-home hospice care, Christina's mom went to be with the Lord on April 1st. We had a really beautiful celebration of life service and have spent a lot of time with family in these last months. We're grateful for the time that we were able to spend with her before she passed and have been heavily involved with the transitions that have come afterwards. Thank you for your prayers for us and our family during this season. There is lots to update you on in our Wycliffe ministry. First, this is a very exciting time to be involved in Bible translation. Through partnerships around the world, more and more people are receiving God's Word in their own language. Earlier this year marked the 800th language to receive a complete Bible. This means that approximately 6.2 billion people in 800 language communities now have access to the complete Word of God. As I continue to support the technology that helps make Bible translation and linguistic work possible, AI has greatly multiplied and accelerated what I'm able to do on a daily basis. What used to take weeks or months, or I couldn't even do, can now be done in days or weeks with better results. Through using AI and modern technology we been able to make vital software resources more accessible for people around the world Whether it instantly translating a global website into dozens of languages or giving people 24-7 access to AI chatbots in almost 100 different languages. Using AI is like having superpowers. We're able to effectively advance the cause of Bible translation and linguistic work around the world. In April, I started a new assignment with Wycliffe, working as a communications specialist. This means I get to use my writing and design skills to help advance the work of Bible translation. Writing travel reports and newsletters, editing internal communications, doing social media posts and video scripts, and designing brochures and flyers. These are some examples of the things I get to do to support the work of Bible translation. Translation work is also accelerating. By 2033, we expect that every single language of the world will have access to at least some portion of God's work. What a pivotal time to be involved in Bible translation. You are helping make this happen through your prayers and financial partnerships. On behalf of dozens of language groups who have recently received God's word in their language, thank you. If you'd like to become more involved in supporting the work of our Wycliffe ministry, or asking the Lord for new and increased monthly financial partners, would you prayerfully consider making an eternal impact by becoming a monthly partner? May God bless you and pour out his favor on you as you seek him and his kingdom. God bless. you",
